-- Housing: Founder's Point (map 2735) static spawns.
--
-- 12.0.1 retail capture data by others. There is no capture of Founder's Point by the owner. Every
-- spawn and template row below comes from agatho/TrinityCore commit 8a4c29d966,
-- sql/housing/world_alliance_neighborhood_spawns.sql, a WowPacketParser dump of
-- dump_12.0.1.65940_2026-02-19_10-35-38.pkt (build 12.0.1.65940). Row comments give the line in that file.
-- VerifiedBuild is 65940 on every row taken from that dump, so the source build stays visible (the addon
-- tables have no such column). The two spell_target_position rows at the end are not from the dump and carry 0.
--
-- Filtered the same way as the Razorwind Shores file: only map 2735; no rows WowPacketParser commented
-- out (creatures riding vehicles or transports); no cornerstones 457142, house doors, House Structure
-- 574432, platform 417487 or ground WMOs (584699 and any other "Ground WMO"), which retail makes per plot
-- or per house; no creatures that retail 12.0.7 only showed with CreatedBy or SummonedBy, and not the
-- player's own steward 249850. That 12.0.1 dump has no entity fragments or CreatedBy values, so those
-- filters work by entry. Nothing that already exists on the live database is deleted or replaced. The steward
-- 249850 still gets the template values of the dump below, because it is the live ender of "My First Home".
--
-- Movement: the dump also holds the movement WowPacketParser recorded for creatures on map 2735. None of it
-- is in this file. No spawn row in the dump carries the retail guid a path was recorded from, so a path could
-- only be tied to a spawn by guessing from distance, and no recorded node has a pause. Every spawn keeps the
-- movement type of the dump: standing, or wandering at random where the dump says so.
--
-- Phases: agatho's dump forced every spawn to phase 0, so there is no phase data at all.
-- The spawns need a map_difficulty row for map 2735, difficulty 0. The 12.1 client MapDifficulty.db2 has none;
-- 2026_13_32_03_hotfixes_housing_map_difficulty.sql adds it on the server. Without it ObjectMgr skips every
-- spawn below as an unsupported difficulty. The Alliance house doors are not in this file: the dump has no
-- template for 575017, 586576 or 602702, and the server makes those templates itself.

SET @CGUID := 13100000;
SET @OGUID := 13100000;
SET @NPCTEXTID := 13100000;

-- 12.0.1 retail capture data by others: gameobject templates missing on the live database


